{"id": "EUVD-2026-103045", "enisaUuid": "0947df77-e0ae-3098-8b0e-b939805b754a", "description": "Xiaozhi-esp32-server-java through 6.1.0 contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows unauthenticated attackers to obtain valid device WebSocket tokens by requesting /api/device/ota with any MAC address. Attackers can open a victim device's WebSocket channel to read private role system prompts, write conversation history, consume LLM/STT/TTS credentials, and overwrite device metadata.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:38:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:38:59", "baseScore": 6.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java-ota-device-token-issuance", "https://github.com/joey-zhou/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java/blob/v6.1.0/xiaozhi-server/src/main/java/com/xiaozhi/device/DeviceAppService.java#L298-L346", "https://github.com/joey-zhou/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java/blob/v6.1.0/xiaozhi-server/src/main/java/com/xiaozhi/device/DeviceController.java#L142-L153", "https://github.com/joey-zhou/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java/blob/v6.1.0/xiaozhi-common/src/main/java/com/xiaozhi/communication/auth/DeviceAuthService.java#L76-L81", "https://github.com/joey-zhou/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/xiaozhi-esp32-server-java-through-6.1.0-authentication-bypass-via-ota-endpoint-token-issuance"], "aliases": ["GHSA-g79m-4gpq-p8x3", "CVE-2026-111623"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.36, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8daa53e4-a99c-34a0-8aae-bc0d8bd38436", "product": {"name": "xiaozhi-esp32-server-java", "vendor": {"name": "joey-zhou"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.1.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "952d39de-9d7b-3359-95b7-e204f73afc65", "vendor": {"name": "joey-zhou"}}], "isExploited": false}